<http://ontology.ipbes.net/report/sch/GA119-6.3.3.1> a ipbes:SubChapter ;
    ipbes:Chapter <http://ontology.ipbes.net/report/ch/GA119ch6> ;
    ipbes:Report ipbes:GA119 ;
    ipbes:SubChapter <http://ontology.ipbes.net/report/sch/GA119-6.3.3> ;
    ipbes:hasDescription "Overarching global policies and processes, including and beyond climate change-related agreements have had major impacts on action to protect marine and coastal biodiversity and ecosystem services (chapter 2.1 and 3). In the present section, we focus on key global agreements that need to be integrated into policy for marine and coastal biodiversity and ecosystem services." ;
    dcterms:identifier "6.3.3.1" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Global Marine and Coastal" .

<http://ontology.ipbes.net/report/il/GA119-FigureSPM.1> a ipbes:Illustration ;
    dcterms:identifier "FigureSPM.1" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Global trends in the capacity of nature to sustain contributions to good quality of" .

<http://ontology.ipbes.net/report/il/GA119-FigureSPM.8> a ipbes:Illustration ;
    ipbes:hasDescription "This figure illustrates three main messages: i) the impacts on biodiversity and on nature’s contributions to people (NCP) are the lowest in the “global sustainability” scenario in nearly all sub-regions, ii) regional differences in impacts are high in the regional competition and economic optimism scenario, and iii) material NCP increase the most in the regional competition and economic optimism scenarios, but this comes at the expense of biodiversity and regulating NCP. Projected impacts are based on a subset of the Shared Socioeconomic Pathway (SSP) scenarios and greenhouse gas emissions trajectories (RCP) developed in support of Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change assessments. This figure does not cover the scenarios that include transformative change that are discussed in Chapter 5." ;
    dcterms:identifier "FigureSPM.8" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Projections of the impacts of land use and climate change on biodiversity and" .

